.TH SUNO-EXPORT 1 "February 2026" "suno-export 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
suno-export \- download, process, and sync Suno tracks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B suno-export
[\fB--version\fR] [\fB--help\fR] <command> [options] [args]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B suno-export
is a CLI for downloading Suno tracks, fetching metadata, processing audio formats,
and running end-to-end sync workflows.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B download
Download tracks, metadata, and images.
.TP
.B sync
Run download and process in one workflow.
.TP
.B process
Run conversion and metadata embedding on an existing input root.
.TP
.B download-images
Download artwork from an explicit list or auto-discover missing images.
.TP
.B list
List tracks by workspace.
.TP
.B workspaces
List available workspaces.
.TP
.B metadata <trackId>
Fetch metadata for one track.
.TP
.B fetch-metadata
Fetch and cache metadata for many tracks (IDs or workspace/date filters).
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh cached tracks for all workspaces.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
For commands that expose \fB--token\fR or \fB--browser\fR, at least one is required.
.SH DATE FILTERS
Commands with creation date filters accept:
.IP \(bu 2
ISO timestamps (example: \fB2026-02-01T12:00:00Z\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Date-only values (\fBYYYY-MM-DD\fR), interpreted as inclusive UTC day bounds.
.SH SONGS METADATA
Authoritative \fBsongs_metadata.json\fR lives on the input side.
Backups are created there.
If \fB--copy-songs-metadata-to-output\fR is provided, a finalized copy is written
to the output side at completion.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBsuno-export download --token TOKEN --output ./downloads\fR
Download tracks to \fB./downloads\fR.
.TP
\fBsuno-export sync --browser http://localhost:9222 --output ./downloads --library ./library\fR
Download then convert into \fB./library\fR.
.TP
\fBsuno-export process -i ./downloads -o ./library --reconvert-missing\fR
Process missing formats from an existing download root.
.TP
\fBsuno-export fetch-metadata --ids id1,id2,id3\fR
Fetch metadata for explicit track IDs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR metaflac (1),
.BR atomicparsley (1)
